+**A computable floor.** Whatever tier is assigned, a task is at least **high** if it changes the logic or output of the core deliverable, touches a protected path, or cannot be undone; and at least **standard** if it changes more than about 10 files or 300 lines. A tier can be raised above its floor, never lowered below it. Judgment sets the tier; the floor stops judgment from under-rating work that is small but dangerous.
